3. Integration restriction

Without prior explicit written authorization from the copyright holder, you
may not use any Covered Materials or a substantial portion of them in an
Integrated Product. This includes copying or adapting PsCanvas Classic code or
assets into a multi-function system module, utility suite, application,
framework, toolkit, service, or another project, whether the Integrated Product
is public or private, open or closed source, free or paid, or commercial or
non-commercial.

This restriction applies even if the Integrated Product keeps attribution,
publishes its source, or uses this same License. Authorization must identify
the authorized person or organization and the permitted product, purpose,
scope, and term.

Using a separate process, APK, dynamic feature, plugin, companion package, or
repository does not by itself make a work standalone. It remains an Integrated
Product if another product presents, brands, manages, installs, updates, or
offers it as one of that product's features.

4. What is not integration

The following do not, by themselves, create an Integrated Product:

a. compiling with build tools or using independently licensed,
   general-purpose third-party dependencies that contain no Covered Materials;
b. having a Standalone Work installed, loaded, hooked, configured, or executed
   by LSPosed, libxposed, Android, ColorOS, PsCanvas, a package manager, or
   another operating-system component;
c. communicating with other software solely through operating-system, public,
   or documented interfaces without incorporating Covered Materials into that
   software; or
d. distributing a compliant, separately installed, independently executable
   Standalone Work on the same store, repository, archive, or medium as other
   software.

These exceptions do not permit copying Covered Materials into a dependency,
platform, host, manager, or other software.

